/-!
# Small completions of genuine nonbinary symplectic extension amalgams

The actual full-extension order bound forces a generalized quadrangle and
exact equality of group orders. The full marked Cartan has exactly two fixed
neighbors at each endpoint, so its canonical Weyl arc closes. The resulting
relation makes the paired completion small and identifies the source group
with the native extension. Transport yields a faithful normal Sp₄ subgroup
and its diagram-preserving extension action, including q = 4 and arbitrary
extension degree. Ambient simplicity gives the pure symplectic group.

This proves the Sp₄(2ⁿ), n > 1 specialization of Aschbacher–Smith
F.4.8/F.4.17/F.4.24, using the nonbinary Cartan route of F.4.10/F.4.16,
printed pp.278–283,287–288 of `refs/quasithin.pdf`. The literal original
normalizer applications are exported in the Chapter6 and Chapter12
symplectic-completion modules. Their genuine extension and order inputs
remain with the earlier-source producer.
-/
